@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Whatever becomes a body is now joined into one paragraph, in the one place a body is chosen rather than at each call site" }
~ Do not lose a commit's extraction to a blank line in a quote

Refusing the whole commit for a blank line throws away work that has already been paid for.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "Answering \"why is this like this?\" was dropped as a product claim." }
~ Drop the claim of answering 'why is this like this?' as a product feature

To focus on the tool's actual capabilities rather than unmet claims.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only." }
~ Assign labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only

To maintain control over the integrity of recorded information.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Staleness is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is." }
~ Detect staleness by item body hash rather than line ranges

To accurately track changes in code identity rather than just line positions.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Review as records. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting writes a withdrawal whose reason unit says why, closing writes a resolution." }
~ Record review as confirmations, withdrawals with reasons, and closures with notes

To keep a comprehensive log of all reviews and decisions made.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It ships its own instrument. `bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from." }
~ Ship its own instrument for benchmarking the model

To provide users with the ability to measure the performance of their chosen models on their own commits.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Two thirds of the commands never call a model. Those are the ones worth your time today: they are deterministic, tested, and cost nothing to run." }
~ Focus on deterministic commands over model-dependent ones

To prioritize commands that are reliable, tested, and cost-effective to run.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The figures are published, naming the model each came from, including the experiments that failed." }
~ Publish figures naming the model each came from, including failed experiments

To provide transparency about which models were tested and their results, including any failures.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Over-production is the failure mode that matters. }
~ Highlight over-production as the failure mode that matters

To emphasize the importance of avoiding unnecessary or excessive output in the tool's operations.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The hook only queues and `--estimate` prices a run before it starts. }
~ Meaningfully price extraction runs before starting them

To inform users about the cost of extraction runs before they start, allowing them to make informed decisions.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. }
~ Label cloned corpora as someone else's claims

To clarify the status of units in cloned corpora, indicating that they are not the tool's own claims.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Research the truncated-change problem before building for it }
~ Research the truncated-change problem before building for it

The commit message states that research was done to understand the truncated-change problem, which is a significant issue affecting 59% of held-out changes.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It now opens with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across an await, a test that builds its own fixture." }
~ Open with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across …

To make the documentation relatable and understandable for Rust developers.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Then what the tool does, shown rather than described, with real output from this repository:" }
~ Show what the tool does rather than describe it.

To provide clear and practical information about the tool's functionality.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/0d79d4a840b4.smy@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model is the operator's choice, never the tool's" }
~ The model is the operator's choice, never the tool's

To leave the selection of the model to the user.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-corpus/src/build.rs@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Whatever becomes a body becomes one paragraph, wherever it came from — a model's rationale, or the overflow of a text too long to be a gist." }
~ Whatever becomes a body is now joined into one paragraph

to keep every word the model wrote and avoid refusing the whole commit for a blank line

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-corpus/src/build.rs@bd1f04710855 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A model's rationale arrives as prose, sometimes with a blank line in it, and smysl refuses a unit whose body holds more than one assertion (SMY-E040). Refusing the whole commit for a blank line would throw away every call that produced it had already been paid for." }
~ A body as smysl's `fine` profile will take it: one paragraph

to ensure that the body is one paragraph and avoid refusal due to multiple assertions

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "the error named a `b3:` uid and nothing else. It now shows the unit's gist and the first lines of its body, which is what identified this bug in a minute after half an hour of not knowing." }
~ The error named a `b3:` uid and nothing else

to improve error identification by showing more information

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "it did not say that the model's answers were already cached. They were, so `cargo smysl extract <rev>` after a fix costs no model calls — it took about a second here. The failure now says so, with the path." }
~ It did not say that the model's answers were already cached

to provide more accurate information about the caching status

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The commit that hit it is recorded, from cache, and a test holds the case." }
~ The commit that hit it is recorded, from cache

to ensure that the commit is recorded even if it was already cached

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The commit that hit it is recorded, from cache, and a test holds the case." }
~ A test holds the case

to verify that the fix works as expected

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Whatever becomes a body is now joined into one paragraph, in the one place a body is chosen rather than at each call site" }
~ Join bodies into one paragraph if they contain a blank line

Refusing the whole commit for a blank line throws away work that has already been paid for.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": the error named a `b3:` uid and nothing else. It now shows the unit's gist and the first lines of its body }
~ Show the unit's gist and the first lines of its body in error messages

It now shows the unit's gist and the first lines of its body, which is what identified this bug in a minute after half an hour of not knowing.

@decision d/gbd1f04710855-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:bd1f047108556a3400ef7659cd8c33272b4452d0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": it did not say that the model's answers were already cached. They were }
~ Indicate that cached answers are used in failure messages

it did not say that the model's answers were already cached. They were, so `cargo smysl extract <rev>` after a fix costs no model calls.

